      <text x="509" y="200" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-weight="600" font-size="13" fill="#f6f4ef">capacity spun up for you</text>
      <text x="509" y="220" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#c99a63">every request, round-trip and billed</text>
      <text x="340" y="292" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="11.5" fill="#81949c">Local inference still uses power. The difference is the trip and the new capacity, not zero energy.</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="figure-cap"><b>Local answer vs metered round-trip.</b> One path stays on your desk. The other bills a warehouse of GPUs for every token.</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endmacro %}

